From 7f1d89873662230acd2b9db1a2e35a6de9277427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: Dolby Vision metadata measured from an HDR10
 picture

An HDR10 video has no dynamic metadata of its studio. For a display that
takes Dolby Vision, Hades can send it as Dolby Vision with metadata that
it measures from the picture as it plays. They are not the studio's and
say so (the setting, the log and the player information): no trims are
made up (there is no colourist's grade to translate), and no level 3
(CCM 001 reserves it).

dvbridge_measure.c measures a picture on the GPU, in two passes over the
reduced pixel set of ST 2094-10:2021 6.1 (2x2 means of R'G'B' from the
10-bit 4:2:0 BT.2020 picture): per block row and column band the max, sum
and min that level 1 is made of, and per block column the max that the
bars are found by. The results are read back without waiting, when their
fence has passed: Kodi measures the pictures queued for presentation ahead
of it, so nothing waits for the GPU and no latency is added.

dvbridge_measured.c decides. Level 1 is over the active area (level 5),
the area of the picture that is ever not black around which the black
edges can be bars (as wide at the top as at the bottom, around at least 40
percent of the picture: a dark picture with a bright spot is no letterbox).
It is held per scene, as Dolby Vision metadata are: the scene so far and
the pictures measured after it that are of it, changing within a scene
only by more than a step. A scene cut is a picture whose 16 x 9 grid of
mean maxRGB differs from the one before by more than 0.05 PQ and by more
than 2.5 times the median of the last 12 differences (motion), and, where
the picture after it is measured too, one that the next picture stays
close to (a step) and does not go back from (a flash is no cut). The cut
refreshes the scene on its own picture. The clamps are dovi_tool's for CM
v2.9, as for HDR10+.

Measured on Cosmos Laundromat (Netflix Open Content, CC BY 4.0, the HDR P3
PQ encode) against the 99 shot cuts of the Dolby Vision metadata that
Dolby's tool made of its master: with one picture or more measured ahead,
96 cuts found on their first picture, 3 missed, 12 made where there is
none; without the look-ahead 98 found and 47 made up (with the first rule,
a threshold alone, 349). Within the shots the level 1 sent changes 699
times in 17520 pictures, against 14446 for a per-picture measurement. The
average sent is 64 codes off the level 1 of each whole shot computed with
full knowledge of it, and the max 290 (the brighter pictures of a shot are
not known before they come, and a cut that is missed joins two shots); no
picture's own max is above the max sent by more than a step, so nothing
is mapped as brighter than it was measured.

dvbridge_profile81_metadata() is the profile 8.1 builder of the HDR10+
path, with a level 5 block; dvbridge_measured_placeholder() and
dvbridge_measured_apply() make the metadata a picture leaves the decoder
with (level 1 from the static metadata) and those it is presented with.
